# Confluence structure

New pages **must** use a cold-reader Markdown body with a short Overview and
headed sections. Do not dump an unheaded prose blob.

```markdown
## Overview

<Why this page exists, who it is for, and the outcome a cold reader should
reach. Brief — not a substitute for the detail sections below.>

## <Section name>

<Durable facts, procedures, or decisions. One job per H2.>

## <Section name>

<...>
```

## Rules

- **Overview** — why, audience, and outcome. Always present on new pages.
- **H2 sections** — one purpose each; stable names a later
  `confluence_update_page_section` can target.
- Prefer short prose and bullets. Avoid markdown Atlassian’s converter
  commonly mangles (nested tables, exotic fences); rewrite in plain prose
  rather than inventing custom clients.
- Do not bury the only actionable content inside Overview alone when the
  page has multiple durable topics — split into H2s.
- Keep titles specific (`Homelab media library layout`, not `Notes`).
- Labels: add only when the user or host convention names them; never invent
  a labeling taxonomy.
